 "parseNotes": [
  "Group \"Advised Electives\" carries a note or open-ended option: \"Advised Electives are designed to allow students to concentrate in areas related to their professional goals. Advised Electives will be planned by the student in consultation with their academic advisor. At least 15 credit hours must be at the 300 level or higher with remaining credit hours being fulfilled by courses at the 200 level or above (exceptions to the 200 level course restriction include BIO 181, BIO 183, and FL* 1** courses that are not in your language of proficiency). Courses used to meet GEP requirements cannot also be used to meet Advised Electives requirements.\"",
  "Group \"Free Electives (12 Hr S/U Lmt)\" carries a note or open-ended option: \"Free Elective courses can NOT be CH 100, C 111, MA 100, MA 101, MA 103, MA 107, MA 108, MA 111, MA 121, MA 131, MA 231, PY 131, PY 211, PY 212, ENG 100. 100-level World Language Courses (WL*) can be used if not satisfying the language proficiency requirement.\""
 ],
